db/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "g(x)=- 2 x^{2} + \\frac{e^{2 x}}{2} - \\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496556} {:answer/id #uuid "57d4f7d9-ed6c-5a97-87e2-d6c53f06b31b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "g(x)=2 x^{2} - \\frac{e^{2 x}}{2} - \\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496564} {:answer/id #uuid "7694c46f-e60d-5d4f-a7ce-be776be3d5ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "g(x)=2 x^{2} - \\frac{e^{2 x}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496570} {:answer/id #uuid "e9cac29f-14b5-5870-adf5-b3a40432c52d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "g(x)=4 x - e^{2 x} - 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496588} {:answer/id #uuid "f021c66e-4c17-5d8b-b6b0-3bdb846a1345" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "g(x)=x^{2} - \\frac{e^{2 x}}{4} - \\frac{7}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496589}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186496564} :answer-field/id #uuid "6f9b219b-9380-5027-899f-fba5ea430d76" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496568}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "afdd11d0-4e3c-5120-9f08-464acb94efd0" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $g'(x)=4 x- e^{2 x}$ that satisfies the condition $g(0)=-2.$" :question/worked-solution "The derivative is already isolated, so we have\n\n$$\ng'(x)=4 x- e^{2 x}.\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x,$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int g'(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (4 x- e^{2 x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ g(x) & =\\int (4 x)\\,\\text{d}x + \\int (- e^{2 x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ & =(4)\\left(\\frac{x^{2}}{2}\\right) + (-1)\\left(\\frac{e^{2 x}}{2}\\right)+C \\\\ & =2 x^{2}- \\frac{e^{2 x}}{2}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo our general solution is $g(x)=2 x^{2}- \\frac{e^{2 x}}{2}+C.$ To find a particular solution, we substitute the condition $g(0)=-2$ into our solution and obtain a value for $C,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2 & =(2 (0)^{2}) + \\left(- \\frac{e^{2 (0)}}{2}\\right)+C \\\\ -2 & =(0) + \\left(- \\frac{1}{2}\\right)+C \\\\ C & =- \\frac{3}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our particular solution is\n\n$$\ng(x)=2 x^{2} - \\frac{e^{2 x}}{2} - \\frac{3}{2}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186496590 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "46a51229-760d-59b7-9713-62d0167e9710" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- 2 x^{3} - 2 \\sin{(x )} - 5 + e^{- 2 x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496561}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186496561} :answer-field/id #uuid "d54af8b6-64e9-50e8-a679-eed9f7d39cf4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496585}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "ff8b0291-a711-56fa-8ba2-9a74a6a7ab1c" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $y'=- 6 x^{2}- 2 e^{- 2 x}- 2 \\cos{(x )}$ that satisfies the condition $y(0)=-4.$\n\n$y=\\,${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The derivative is already isolated, so we have\n\n$$\ny'=- 6 x^{2}- 2 e^{- 2 x}- 2 \\cos{(x )}.\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x,$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int y'\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (- 6 x^{2}- 2 e^{- 2 x}- 2 \\cos{(x )})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =\\int (- 6 x^{2})\\,\\text{d}x + \\int (- 2 e^{- 2 x})\\,\\text{d}x + \\int (- 2 \\cos{(x )})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ & =(-6)\\left(\\frac{x^{3}}{3}\\right) + (-2)\\left(- \\frac{e^{- 2 x}}{2}\\right) + (-2)(\\sin{(x )})+C \\\\ & =- 2 x^{3}+e^{- 2 x}- 2 \\sin{(x )}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo our general solution is $y=- 2 x^{3}+e^{- 2 x}- 2 \\sin{(x )}+C.$ To find a particular solution, we substitute the condition $y(0)=-4$ into our solution and obtain a value for $C,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4 & =(- 2 (0)^{3}) + (e^{- 2 (0)}) + (- 2 \\sin{((0) )})+C \\\\ -4 & =(0) + (1) + (0)+C \\\\ C & =-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our particular solution is\n\n$$\ny=- 2 x^{3} - 2 \\sin{(x )} - 5 + e^{- 2 x}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186497386 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "466436a8-4af6-538b-9c6f-dc9fef31373c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4{e}^{3x}-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496811} {:answer/id #uuid "55bfbd25-7cd4-58e5-9f38-dc990ba4a925" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-{e}^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496840} {:answer/id #uuid "d0f48d39-9abb-58ad-92f4-b282755cf973" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1-2{e}^{3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497093} {:answer/id #uuid "d8339946-1b5f-5196-bce2-e29dceabf2f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2{e}^{3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497113} {:answer/id #uuid "f715f065-06d5-5837-ae98-a58247ced1f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{e}^{x}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497187}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186497113} :answer-field/id #uuid "fcb0452a-b540-5991-8720-5551a36772ac" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497321}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "a6522825-4faa-5281-807b-1fb4ff06c302" :question/math-academy-id "q-129799" :question/problem "Compute the Wronskian $W({y}_{1},{y}_{2})$ for ${y}_{1}(x)=2{e}^{x}$ and ${y}_{2}(x)={e}^{2x}.$" :question/worked-solution "The Wronskian $W({y}_{1},{y}_{2})$ of two functions ${y}_{1}(x)$ and ${y}_{2}(x)$ is defined as\n\n$$\nW({y}_{1},{y}_{2})=\\begin{vmatrix}{y}_{1} & {y}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{1}^{′} & {y}_{2}^{′}\\end{vmatrix}={y}_{1}{y}_{2}^{′}-{y}_{2}{y}_{1}^{′}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have ${y}_{1}(x)=2{e}^{x}$ and ${y}_{2}(x)={e}^{2x}.$ Therefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}W({y}_{1},{y}_{2}) & =(2{e}^{x}){({e}^{2x})}^{′}-({e}^{2x}){(2{e}^{x})}^{′} \\\\  & =(2{e}^{x})(2{e}^{2x})-({e}^{2x})(2{e}^{x}) \\\\  & ={4}^{3x}-2{e}^{3x} \\\\  & =2{e}^{3x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186503728 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3d7a6d1e-b67a-5086-8d8e-bc807158948a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{e}^{-6x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503095} {:answer/id #uuid "4e1371dc-c00c-5e29-9079-f6bee21cefbf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{e}^{-1-2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503131} {:answer/id #uuid "96581053-e51a-57c0-91dc-cdedecceb889" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "5{e}^{-2x}+2{e}^{-4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503276} {:answer/id #uuid "e52cdcee-ace6-5887-9332-30bbc7af4b46" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{e}^{6-4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503450} {:answer/id #uuid "eca2abbd-fc58-5d08-8f21-69f9b411e1fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{e}^{-2x}+{e}^{-4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503465}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186503095} :answer-field/id #uuid "8ea658b1-8a5c-53c8-b110-9aef693ebefd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503585}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "ac3ed9ab-9e20-50c1-a2df-d0e7acffd405" :question/math-academy-id "q-90726" :question/problem "Given that $y=y(x)$ satisfies the equation ${y}^{″}+6{y}^{′}+8y=0,$ which of the following **cannot** be $y(x)?$" :question/worked-solution "Assuming $y={e}^{\\lambda x}$ and differentiating $y$ with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x},\\,{y}^{″}={\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}+6\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x}+8{e}^{\\lambda x} & =0 \\\\ {e}^{\\lambda x}({\\lambda }^{2}+6\\lambda +8) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation is therefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}+6\\lambda +8 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFactoring the auxiliary equation results in\n\n$$\n(\\lambda +2)(\\lambda +4)=0,\n$$\n\nand so the solutions of the auxiliary equation  are $\\lambda =-2$ or $\\lambda =-4.$\n\nTherefore, any linear combination of the functions ${e}^{-2x}$ and ${e}^{-4x}$ is a solution to the original differential equation. \n\nAmong the given options, only ${e}^{-6x}$ is not a solution."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186514385 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c73650fb-8ca5-5747-bbe3-f451e92a6a69" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-2e^{-4\\sin x}\\cos x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514054}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186514054} :answer-field/id #uuid "bb0216fd-fe08-5818-afd9-7fc21cfab6bb" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514312}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "2d877a64-29c8-5e32-8920-d62abb73e697" :question/math-academy-id "q-166076" :question/problem "Given that $y=f(h(x)),$ calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that $y$ is a composite function:\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{h},\\,h=-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}h}=\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{h},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}h}{\\text{d}x}=-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}h}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}h}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{h}\\cdot (-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡x) \\\\  & =-2{e}^{-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\  & =-\\frac{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{{e}^{4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186514423 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "569b842d-17a2-53d4-9b00-9b5178c0a749" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2e^x+12x^2-\\frac{x^4}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513767}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186513767} :answer-field/id #uuid "9a994c66-aac8-5b19-bc23-3cf37a49b2cc" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514300}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "7323da16-6dcc-5329-81f1-5b6cb91bd332" :question/math-academy-id "q-166079" :question/problem "$$\n\\displaystyle \\int (4f(x)+3g(x))\\,\\text{d}x\\,=\n$${{field-1}}\n$+C,\\,$ where $C$ is an arbitrary constant." :question/worked-solution "We combine the sum and the constant multiple rules, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (4f(x)+3g(x))\\text{d}x & =\\int (4\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}{e}^{x}+3(8x-\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{3}))\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (2{e}^{x}+24x-2{x}^{3})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\int {e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x+24\\int x\\,\\text{d}x-2\\int {x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2{e}^{x}+24\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}-2\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}+C \\\\  & =2{e}^{x}-\\frac{{x}^{4}}{2}+12{x}^{2}+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an arbitrary constant."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186520457 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0bd0f410-6e9b-5a13-84b6-2793313eb013" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}-3}{\\sqrt{({x}^{3}-2x)^{3}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520005} {:answer/id #uuid "0e0c3af3-091e-560d-ac8e-abe55cc9d0f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{3{x}^{2}-2}{\\sqrt{({x}^{3}-2x)^{3}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520009} {:answer/id #uuid "75d7df1e-163d-51cf-9003-0d07b95639d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{3{x}^{2}-2}{\\sqrt{{x}^{3}-2x}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520161} {:answer/id #uuid "86d89cd3-8e55-5f29-83ed-c409f606d553" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{2{x}^{2}-3}{\\sqrt{{x}^{3}-2x}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520189} {:answer/id #uuid "996b8fd1-b20a-565b-98d1-c22e6ee7d68a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{{x}^{2}+3}{\\sqrt{({x}^{3}-2x)^{3}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520208}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186520009} :answer-field/id #uuid "686cff4f-8265-5ba3-8560-bcdf5671d8d5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520397}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "321f22b7-0ca5-594c-82a7-c5cf5cf23fad" :question/math-academy-id "q-71952" :question/problem "Find ${f}^{′}(x)$ for $f(x)=\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{{x}^{3}-2x}}.$" :question/worked-solution "Let $g(x)={x}^{3}-2x$ and $f(g(x))=\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{g}}=2{g}^{-1/2}.$ \n\nDifferentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(g(x)) & =2({g}^{-1/2})^{′}=-2\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}{g}^{-3/2}=-\\frac{1}{{g}^{3/2}}, \\\\ {g}^{′}(x) & =({x}^{3}-2x)^{′}=3{x}^{2}-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, using the chain rule, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={f}^{′}(g(x))\\cdot {g}^{′}(x) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{{g}^{3/2}}\\cdot (3{x}^{2}-2) \\\\  & =-\\frac{3{x}^{2}-2}{{g}^{3/2}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3{x}^{2}-2}{\\sqrt{({x}^{3}-2x)^{3}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186520473 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1bf96aed-c4c2-50a0-9312-269557ced95f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "8(1-3x)^{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520029} {:answer/id #uuid "4793072d-d61e-5f93-bb0c-993627ee72c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-24(1+3x)^{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520100} {:answer/id #uuid "99709777-eb56-5d41-ac58-1c43410ac856" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-24(1-3x)^{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520209} {:answer/id #uuid "d2298536-2087-59b8-a435-384b956031dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "24(1+3x)^{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520286} {:answer/id #uuid "e7514498-fddf-54d8-9478-ff10ceb72766" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-3(1-3x)^{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520330}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186520209} :answer-field/id #uuid "44da7608-9cb4-57b2-9694-53ee352f7833" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520387}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "73597027-954f-5bff-8c64-de058a3fe822" :question/math-academy-id "q-107296" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)={(1-3x)}^{8},$ find ${f}^{′}(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Let $g(x)=1-3x$ and $f(g(x))=g(x)^{8}.$ \n\nDifferentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(g(x)) & =({g}^{8})^{′}=8{g}^{7}, \\\\ {g}^{′}(x) & =(1-3x)^{′}=-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, using the chain rule, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={f}^{′}(g(x))\\cdot {g}^{′}(x) \\\\  & =8{g}^{7}\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & =-24(1-3x)^{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186520484 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6e10ad36-36ec-5632-8f07-eff850b3becf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4x^{3}-9x^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520153}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186520153} :answer-field/id #uuid "8b7fd03c-605a-5e8e-8867-8d3e258ab8cf" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520410}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "930f9486-b8c5-5ccf-b917-a4806acde6bf" :question/math-academy-id "q-314207" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)={({x}^{4}-3{x}^{3})}^{2},$ find ${f}^{′}(x).$\n\n${f}^{′}(x)=2({x}^{4}-3{x}^{3})($\n{{field-1}}\n$)$" :question/worked-solution "Let $g(x)={x}^{4}-3{x}^{3}$ and $f(g(x))=g(x)^{2}.$ \n\nDifferentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(g(x)) & =({g}^{2})^{′}=2g, \\\\ {g}^{′}(x) & =({x}^{4}-3{x}^{3})^{′}=4{x}^{3}-9{x}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, using the chain rule, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={f}^{′}(g(x))\\cdot {g}^{′}(x) \\\\  & =2g\\cdot (4{x}^{3}-9{x}^{2}) \\\\  & =2({x}^{4}-3{x}^{3})(\\,4{x}^{3}-9{x}^{2}\\,).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
